# Cross-domain isomorphism (planning)

When planning, researching, or weighing Adopt/Refuse across domains, follow skill
**cross-domain-isomorphism** (`.cursor/skills/cross-domain-isomorphism/SKILL.md`).

Hard split: **Structure-Adopt** (shared algebra → algorithm/pattern/sensor/docs) vs
**Substrate-Refuse** (wetware/ASIC/medium as tip merge/citation SoT without Spec).

Before importing or dismissing a distant field, run **I1–I5**: name objects/morphisms;
cite CS landing; state non-preserved; choose typed artefact; default **no** boolean
SoT retype. One-line habit:

`Iso: A ≅ B → land as <type> | non-preserved: … | I5: no SoT retype`

Do not soften fail_under / citation SoT via free-energy, Landauer, PID, entropy, or
“chemistry already computes.” Steal algebra; keep predicate types; leave the dish/chip
off tip unless Spec changes product category.

